1
00:00:01,124 --> 00:00:05,999
-(Todo yelling)
-(punches thudding)

2
00:00:11,916 --> 00:00:13,459
[Todo] When I was in third grade

3
00:00:13,541 --> 00:00:16,417
I beat up a cocky
high school kid.

4
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:19,125
(kid groaning)

5
00:00:21,293 --> 00:00:24,209
Even if he was older,
cocky is still cocky.

6
00:00:25,501 --> 00:00:27,168
The kid was mockin' me!

7
00:00:27,251 --> 00:00:29,001
(bird calling)

8
00:00:29,084 --> 00:00:31,084
(hand scraping)

9
00:00:31,168 --> 00:00:33,126
And when I feel mocked, well,

10
00:00:33,209 --> 00:00:36,419
that's as good as a
starting bell in the ring!

11
00:00:37,710 --> 00:00:38,502
It wasn't even that fun.

12
00:00:38,585 --> 00:00:40,918
I found out that
trouncing a boring guy

13
00:00:41,002 --> 00:00:42,294
was naturally boring too.

14
00:00:42,377 --> 00:00:45,294
-(Todo sighing)
-(intense rock music)

15
00:00:45,377 --> 00:00:46,127
[Yuki] Nice fight, boy!

16
00:00:46,210 --> 00:00:48,128
[Todo] Huh?

17
00:00:50,044 --> 00:00:51,128
So, when it comes to women,

18
00:00:53,544 --> 00:00:54,544
what's your type?

19
00:00:55,919 --> 00:00:56,836
What the?

20
00:00:56,919 --> 00:00:58,044
Who are you?

21
00:00:58,128 --> 00:00:59,170
(Yuki chuckling)

22
00:00:59,253 --> 00:01:00,336
One look at her and I knew.

23
00:01:00,420 --> 00:01:03,129
My boring world was about
to be flipped upside-down.

24
00:01:06,587 --> 00:01:09,754
(opening theme music)

25
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:15,504
(singer singing in Japanese)

26
00:02:35,469 --> 00:02:38,843
(air whistling)

27
00:02:47,344 --> 00:02:49,304
The time to unleash my
technique has finally come!

28
00:02:49,344 --> 00:02:50,261
Huh?

29
00:02:50,344 --> 00:02:52,470
Didn't you use it before?

30
00:02:52,552 --> 00:02:54,262
Look, in our current situation,

31
00:02:54,345 --> 00:02:56,970
I don't have time to
explain my technique to you!

32
00:02:57,053 --> 00:03:00,262
There's really only one
piece of advice I can give you.

33
00:03:00,345 --> 00:03:01,429
Don't stop!

34
00:03:02,262 --> 00:03:03,845
And believe in me!

35
00:03:03,928 --> 00:03:04,845
Okay!

36
00:03:04,928 --> 00:03:06,429
But that's two.

37
00:03:06,512 --> 00:03:08,013
(pensive rock music)

38
00:03:08,096 --> 00:03:10,430
[Todo] Let's examine the
cards our opponent's holding.

39
00:03:10,513 --> 00:03:13,846
One is roots that
emerge from the ground.

40
00:03:13,929 --> 00:03:15,449
That one probably
gains power and speed

41
00:03:15,513 --> 00:03:18,472
the more it limits
quantity and range.

42
00:03:19,929 --> 00:03:22,097
Then there's Wooden Ball.

43
00:03:22,181 --> 00:03:24,365
Each ball can attack once or
twice and then it's expended.

44
00:03:24,389 --> 00:03:26,431
They can remain airborne

45
00:03:26,514 --> 00:03:29,306
and we have to watch
out for delayed activation.

46
00:03:29,389 --> 00:03:32,847
Then there's Cursed Bud, that's
probably what got Fushiguro.

47
00:03:32,930 --> 00:03:34,407
I guess you're out if even
if one of those hits you,

48
00:03:34,431 --> 00:03:36,515
though I wanna
believe that means

49
00:03:36,598 --> 00:03:38,848
it can't fire too many of them.

50
00:03:38,931 --> 00:03:42,140
As for Flower Field, it
looks like that relaxes you,

51
00:03:42,223 --> 00:03:44,515
but its earlier wounds
are throwing it off now,

52
00:03:44,598 --> 00:03:46,681
so no need to worry about that.

53
00:03:46,765 --> 00:03:48,433
Then there's that
unleashed left arm

54
00:03:48,516 --> 00:03:50,724
and the possibility
it's just a bluff.

55
00:03:51,932 --> 00:03:53,849
However, it doesn't
matter what a technique is

56
00:03:53,932 --> 00:03:56,224
if you don't let
them activate it!

57
00:03:56,308 --> 00:04:00,141
So even accounting for
unexpected situations,

58
00:04:00,224 --> 00:04:00,682
(air whooshing)

59
00:04:00,766 --> 00:04:05,517
my 530,000 IQ mental CPU

60
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:06,683
(text chiming)

61
00:04:06,767 --> 00:04:08,267
(neurons crackling)

62
00:04:08,350 --> 00:04:13,100
produces only one
inescapable conclusion:

63
00:04:15,767 --> 00:04:16,934
victory!

64
00:04:17,435 --> 00:04:19,559
-♪ Oh ♪
-♪ Oh oh oh oh ♪

65
00:04:19,642 --> 00:04:20,518
Because I'm not alone, brother!

66
00:04:20,601 --> 00:04:23,185
Because you're here!

67
00:04:23,268 --> 00:04:25,268
-♪ Oh oh oh oh ♪
-(footsteps thundering)

68
00:04:25,351 --> 00:04:27,185
And you're with me!

69
00:04:27,268 --> 00:04:28,893
(root whipping)

70
00:04:28,976 --> 00:04:29,977
Huh?

71
00:04:30,977 --> 00:04:31,352
(Hanami scoffing)

72
00:04:31,436 --> 00:04:35,102
(Todo yelling)

73
00:04:36,810 --> 00:04:37,727
Todo!

74
00:04:37,810 --> 00:04:38,894
(Yuji panting)

75
00:04:38,977 --> 00:04:40,727
(Todo yelling)

76
00:04:40,810 --> 00:04:43,727
-(Todo grunting)
-(Todo crashing)

77
00:04:43,811 --> 00:04:44,561
(gasping) Todo!

78
00:04:44,644 --> 00:04:46,353
-(Yuji grunting)
-(blows thudding)

79
00:04:46,437 --> 00:04:47,353
(air whooshing)

80
00:04:47,437 --> 00:04:49,686
[Hanami] That's one down.

81
00:04:50,811 --> 00:04:52,228
(Todo clapping)

82
00:04:52,312 --> 00:04:55,020
(blood splatting)

83
00:04:57,061 --> 00:04:58,396
(Hanami gurgling)

84
00:04:58,480 --> 00:05:00,480
(Yuji sputtering)

85
00:05:00,562 --> 00:05:02,104
(air whooshing)

86
00:05:02,188 --> 00:05:03,604
Whoa, Todo?

87
00:05:03,687 --> 00:05:04,937
[Hanami] I see.

88
00:05:05,021 --> 00:05:07,313
It's simple, and yet therefore

89
00:05:07,396 --> 00:05:10,229
it's a troubling
technique you have.

90
00:05:10,313 --> 00:05:11,563
Yes.

91
00:05:11,646 --> 00:05:15,397
It's simply swapping my
position for that of my opponent's.

92
00:05:15,481 --> 00:05:17,397
The Boogie Woogie!

93
00:05:17,481 --> 00:05:18,355
(Yuji gasping)

94
00:05:18,439 --> 00:05:20,980
-Todo- -Shh!

95
00:05:21,063 --> 00:05:23,105
I will end this
before it can adapt.

96
00:05:23,189 --> 00:05:24,189
(Todo chuckling)

97
00:05:24,230 --> 00:05:25,230
(Todo growling)

98
00:05:25,314 --> 00:05:26,315
(footsteps thundering)

99
00:05:26,398 --> 00:05:28,564
By the way, (clapping)

100
00:05:28,647 --> 00:05:29,981
clapping my hands (clapping)

101
00:05:30,064 --> 00:05:31,606
is necessary to activate it!

102
00:05:31,689 --> 00:05:32,773
(Todo clapping)

103
00:05:32,856 --> 00:05:34,249
-(air whooshing)
-(footsteps thudding)

104
00:05:34,273 --> 00:05:35,582
-(Yuji and Todo grunting)
-(blows thudding)

105
00:05:35,606 --> 00:05:36,523
(Todo clapping)

106
00:05:36,606 --> 00:05:37,874
-(Yuji and Todo grunting)
-(blows thudding)

107
00:05:37,898 --> 00:05:39,441
(Todo clapping) [Hanami] Huh?

108
00:05:39,524 --> 00:05:41,232
(Todo clapping)

109
00:05:41,316 --> 00:05:43,607
-(Yuji grunting)
-(blows thudding)

110
00:05:43,690 --> 00:05:44,483
-(Todo grunting)
-(blows thudding)

111
00:05:44,565 --> 00:05:46,815
(Hanami hissing)

112
00:05:46,899 --> 00:05:47,774
Their builds are too different!

113
00:05:47,857 --> 00:05:50,399
There's a big change
every time they swap!

114
00:05:51,524 --> 00:05:52,524
(Todo clapping)

115
00:05:52,565 --> 00:05:54,126
-(Yuji and Todo grunting)
-(blows thudding)

116
00:05:54,150 --> 00:05:55,525
Is he swapping with me

117
00:05:55,608 --> 00:05:57,400
or is he swapping
with Sukuna's vessel?

118
00:05:57,484 --> 00:05:59,775
Every time he claps,

119
00:05:59,858 --> 00:06:02,066
that split-second decision
makes my thoughts falter!

120
00:06:03,233 --> 00:06:04,150
(Todo clapping)

121
00:06:04,233 --> 00:06:05,775
(air whooshing)

122
00:06:05,858 --> 00:06:06,775
-(Yuji grunting)
-(blow thudding)

123
00:06:06,858 --> 00:06:08,234
(Hanami groaning)

124
00:06:08,318 --> 00:06:09,234
Oh no!

125
00:06:09,318 --> 00:06:10,650
I can't, I can't!

126
00:06:10,734 --> 00:06:11,650
(Todo clapping)

127
00:06:11,734 --> 00:06:12,984
(blow thudding)

128
00:06:13,067 --> 00:06:14,193
(Todo clapping)

129
00:06:14,276 --> 00:06:15,859
-(Yuji grunting)
-(blow thudding)

130
00:06:15,942 --> 00:06:19,443
-(Todo grunting)
-(blows thudding)

131
00:06:19,526 --> 00:06:20,626
-(Yuji grunting)
-(blow thudding)

132
00:06:20,650 --> 00:06:21,985
(Todo clapping)

133
00:06:22,068 --> 00:06:22,527
-(Yuji and Todo grunting)
-(blows thudding)

134
00:06:22,610 --> 00:06:25,110
(Hanami groaning)

135
00:06:25,194 --> 00:06:27,902
(Todo clapping)

136
00:06:28,943 --> 00:06:29,568
I can't break out of this!

137
00:06:29,651 --> 00:06:30,527
-(Todo grunting)
-(blow thudding)

138
00:06:30,610 --> 00:06:32,818
(Hanami yelping)

139
00:06:32,902 --> 00:06:35,528
(air whooshing)

140
00:06:35,611 --> 00:06:36,403
(Hanami gasping)

141
00:06:36,487 --> 00:06:38,611
They're using that again!

142
00:06:41,778 --> 00:06:45,195
Using Black Flash consecutively
isn't anything amazing.

143
00:06:45,278 --> 00:06:46,195
(cup clinking)

144
00:06:46,278 --> 00:06:48,569
(gentle pensive music)

145
00:06:48,653 --> 00:06:50,653
Although I find it
is difficult, for me,

146
00:06:50,737 --> 00:06:54,862
to do it more than twice in a
row or on the following day.

147
00:06:54,945 --> 00:06:57,112
It doesn't matter if
the first one is landed

148
00:06:57,196 --> 00:07:01,362
by skill or by a fluke, once
sorcerers land a Black Flash,

149
00:07:01,446 --> 00:07:02,905
they temporarily enter a state

150
00:07:02,988 --> 00:07:05,738
that athletes
commonly call the zone.

151
00:07:05,821 --> 00:07:06,696
The manipulation
of cursed energy

152
00:07:06,780 --> 00:07:08,447
that they normally
control consciously

153
00:07:08,530 --> 00:07:10,530
then becomes as
natural as breathing,

154
00:07:10,613 --> 00:07:13,113
and then there's a
sense of omnipotence

155
00:07:13,197 --> 00:07:15,071
that makes it seem
as if everything else

156
00:07:15,155 --> 00:07:16,697
revolves around them.

157
00:07:16,781 --> 00:07:17,981
I guess that's how I'd put it.

158
00:07:19,655 --> 00:07:22,531
You wanna know
what my record is?

159
00:07:22,614 --> 00:07:25,906
(Nanami sighing)

160
00:07:25,989 --> 00:07:27,114
Four times.

161
00:07:28,156 --> 00:07:29,655
But really I just got lucky.

162
00:07:31,324 --> 00:07:34,573
-(Yuji grunting)
-(intense rock music)

163
00:07:34,656 --> 00:07:36,615
(blow booming)

164
00:07:36,698 --> 00:07:37,740
[Yuji] Black Flash!

165
00:07:39,282 --> 00:07:41,615
[Todo] Brother, I keep having
a premonition about you!

166
00:07:41,698 --> 00:07:45,283
-(Hanami groaning)
-(energy crackling)

167
00:07:45,366 --> 00:07:46,908
(Hanami screaming)

168
00:07:46,991 --> 00:07:48,574
(air whooshing)

169
00:07:48,657 --> 00:07:50,492
(blow crashing)

170
00:07:50,574 --> 00:07:51,699
[Yuji] Black Flash!

171
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:55,574
-(Hanami groaning)
-(blood splatting)

172
00:07:55,657 --> 00:07:56,657
(energy crackling)

173
00:07:56,741 --> 00:07:57,783
Black Flash!

174
00:07:57,866 --> 00:07:59,909
[Todo] Three in a row?

175
00:08:00,825 --> 00:08:03,367
[Hanami] Don't get cocky!

176
00:08:03,451 --> 00:08:04,634
-(air whooshing)
-(Hanami gasping)

177
00:08:04,658 --> 00:08:05,909
Swapping positions?

178
00:08:05,992 --> 00:08:08,117
So what I have to
watch out for now

179
00:08:08,201 --> 00:08:09,117
(Todo clapping)

180
00:08:09,201 --> 00:08:10,326
is Sukuna's vessel!

181
00:08:12,243 --> 00:08:13,410
They didn't swap?

182
00:08:13,494 --> 00:08:17,785
-(air whooshing)
-(energetic rock music)

183
00:08:17,868 --> 00:08:18,785
Just 'cause I clap my hands

184
00:08:18,868 --> 00:08:22,327
doesn't always mean I'm
activating my technique!

185
00:08:22,410 --> 00:08:25,786
It's simple, but
it's easy to fall for.

186
00:08:27,036 --> 00:08:28,436
I keep getting that
same premonition

187
00:08:29,911 --> 00:08:32,619
of my boredom being
turned upside-down!

188
00:08:32,702 --> 00:08:35,453
(blow crashing)

189
00:08:36,619 --> 00:08:38,994
[Yuji] Black Flash!

190
00:08:39,077 --> 00:08:41,745
(energetic music)

191
00:08:43,620 --> 00:08:48,245
(discordant energetic music)

192
00:08:49,412 --> 00:08:51,995
(leaves rustling)

193
00:08:52,078 --> 00:08:53,329
(air whooshing)

194
00:08:53,413 --> 00:08:54,662
(energetic pensive music)

195
00:08:54,746 --> 00:08:56,829
(air whooshing)

196
00:08:56,913 --> 00:08:59,788
(footsteps thundering)

197
00:08:59,871 --> 00:09:02,163
-(Yuji grunting)
-(Wooden Ball shattering)

198
00:09:02,246 --> 00:09:03,555
-(Todo grunting)
-(Wooden Ball shattering)

199
00:09:03,579 --> 00:09:08,080
-(Todo grunting)
-(blows thudding)

200
00:09:08,830 --> 00:09:09,997
(Todo clapping)

201
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:10,997
-(Yuji grunting)
-(blow thudding)

202
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:11,997
-(Yuji grunting)
-Huh?

203
00:09:12,080 --> 00:09:14,580
(roots booming)

204
00:09:15,830 --> 00:09:18,498
♪ Sometimes I
might make you cry ♪

205
00:09:18,580 --> 00:09:20,206
♪ Not on purpose ♪

206
00:09:20,289 --> 00:09:21,373
(Hanami grunting)

207
00:09:21,457 --> 00:09:22,998
(Todo clapping)

208
00:09:23,081 --> 00:09:25,415
-(Todo grunting)
-(roots thudding)

209
00:09:25,499 --> 00:09:26,998
(Yuji grunting)

210
00:09:27,081 --> 00:09:31,873
-(blows thudding)
-(Yuji grunting)

211
00:09:31,956 --> 00:09:34,040
[Yuji] It's attacking
before each swap!

212
00:09:34,123 --> 00:09:36,665
It's getting used to Todo's
technique and adapting!

213
00:09:37,957 --> 00:09:40,707
[Todo] Ah, but that
Black Flash hurt it!

214
00:09:40,791 --> 00:09:44,249
We can exorcize it, together!

215
00:09:45,665 --> 00:09:46,916
[Hanami] This is the first time

216
00:09:46,999 --> 00:09:49,125
I've ever been hurt
so badly in a fight,

217
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,000
and yet, despite that,

218
00:09:52,917 --> 00:09:54,292
(ground rumbling)

219
00:09:54,375 --> 00:09:56,917
my delight in this
battle is only growing!

220
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:01,917
-(Cursed Buds chattering)
-(tense music)

221
00:10:05,126 --> 00:10:06,126
(air whooshing)

222
00:10:06,168 --> 00:10:09,876
-(Cursed Buds chattering)
-(Cursed Buds whooshing)

223
00:10:09,959 --> 00:10:11,918
(Todo clapping)

224
00:10:12,001 --> 00:10:12,918
(Yuji grunting)

225
00:10:13,001 --> 00:10:16,084
(air whooshing)

226
00:10:16,168 --> 00:10:18,710
His technique
reveal was full of lies!

227
00:10:18,794 --> 00:10:21,627
Now it turns out he's able
to swap two others as well?

228
00:10:23,336 --> 00:10:24,336
Todo!

229
00:10:25,503 --> 00:10:26,752
He's protecting me!

230
00:10:26,835 --> 00:10:29,169
[Todo] Don't worry, Brother!

231
00:10:30,002 --> 00:10:33,920
By seriously hardening my
body and my cursed energy,

232
00:10:35,170 --> 00:10:37,295
I'll easily repel these buds!

233
00:10:37,378 --> 00:10:42,128
-(energy whooshing)
-(tense music)

234
00:10:43,462 --> 00:10:44,670
(door rattling)

235
00:10:44,754 --> 00:10:45,670
Huh?

236
00:10:45,754 --> 00:10:46,962
Are you sure of that?

237
00:10:47,046 --> 00:10:49,296
(pensive music)

238
00:10:49,379 --> 00:10:51,837
(gasping) Ta...

239
00:10:51,921 --> 00:10:52,837
Takada?

240
00:10:52,921 --> 00:10:54,463
(dreamy chiming)

241
00:10:54,546 --> 00:10:57,505
You remember Fushiguro's
injuries from those buds?

242
00:10:58,671 --> 00:10:59,671
Of course I do!

243
00:10:59,755 --> 00:11:02,130
In just a matter of seconds,
those same Cursed Buds

244
00:11:02,214 --> 00:11:03,130
are gonna be
slamming right into me!

245
00:11:03,214 --> 00:11:06,797
Then think, Fushiguro's
Buds had grown larger

246
00:11:06,880 --> 00:11:08,838
by the time he
was rescued, right?

247
00:11:08,922 --> 00:11:12,548
(Todo gasping)

248
00:11:13,798 --> 00:11:16,340
You're assuming they
grew by absorbing his blood

249
00:11:16,423 --> 00:11:17,839
and that is possible, of course,

250
00:11:17,923 --> 00:11:21,798
but you're facing
a cursed spirit here.

251
00:11:21,881 --> 00:11:24,631
So what's the
most likely answer?

252
00:11:24,714 --> 00:11:27,216
(clock ticking)

253
00:11:27,882 --> 00:11:30,632
(snapping) Cursed energy!

254
00:11:30,715 --> 00:11:32,174
(text chiming)

255
00:11:32,257 --> 00:11:33,715
(energy whooshing)

256
00:11:33,799 --> 00:11:34,715
(Todo chuckling)

257
00:11:34,799 --> 00:11:38,549
(Cursed Buds thudding)

258
00:11:38,632 --> 00:11:39,508
(Hanami gasping)

259
00:11:39,590 --> 00:11:41,151
[Hanami] He dispelled
his cursed energy!

260
00:11:41,217 --> 00:11:42,716
And right before impact.

261
00:11:42,800 --> 00:11:44,342
He must have figured it out.

262
00:11:44,425 --> 00:11:46,509
The harder they defend
with cursed energy,

263
00:11:46,591 --> 00:11:48,342
the stronger those Buds become!

264
00:11:49,758 --> 00:11:51,425
Her next event is the national.

265
00:11:51,509 --> 00:11:53,884
-(text chiming)
-(Todo grunting)

266
00:11:53,967 --> 00:11:56,426
I'll have to be sure to
thank her then, yeah?

267
00:11:58,134 --> 00:12:00,842
-(Yuji grunting)
-(blows thudding)

268
00:12:00,926 --> 00:12:02,051
(Yuji grunting)

269
00:12:02,134 --> 00:12:03,218
(Todo grunting)

270
00:12:03,301 --> 00:12:05,176
-(blow crashing)
-(Hanami screaming)

271
00:12:05,259 --> 00:12:07,218
♪ Should burn up ♪

272
00:12:07,301 --> 00:12:08,843
Hey, special-grade
cursed spirit!

273
00:12:08,927 --> 00:12:11,427
By now I'm sure you've realized

274
00:12:11,511 --> 00:12:13,469
that I didn't tell you
everything before,

275
00:12:15,469 --> 00:12:18,385
and now there's one more thing
you should be thinking about:

276
00:12:19,093 --> 00:12:21,844
what counts as a target
for Boogie Woogie!

277
00:12:23,928 --> 00:12:27,386
What things can I swap in
the range of my technique?

278
00:12:27,470 --> 00:12:29,428
Only other creatures?

279
00:12:29,512 --> 00:12:30,303
Mais non!

280
00:12:30,386 --> 00:12:32,886
My technique works
on cursed corpses

281
00:12:32,969 --> 00:12:35,053
and inanimate objects too!

282
00:12:35,136 --> 00:12:37,262
So the answer is:

283
00:12:37,346 --> 00:12:39,845
anything possessing cursed
energy above a certain level!

284
00:12:41,678 --> 00:12:43,429
(Todo grunting)

285
00:12:43,513 --> 00:12:46,804
Hey, special-grade cursed
spirit, have you noticed?

286
00:12:46,887 --> 00:12:49,514
We're back at that spot again.

287
00:12:50,971 --> 00:12:53,638
Which means this is
where it lies waiting!

288
00:12:53,721 --> 00:12:54,638
(Todo clapping)

289
00:12:54,721 --> 00:12:55,805
(chains rattling)

290
00:12:55,888 --> 00:12:57,888
(Hanami gasping)

291
00:12:57,971 --> 00:12:58,971
(air whooshing)

292
00:12:59,013 --> 00:13:02,805
Look in the riverbed for
Maki's special-grade tool

293
00:13:04,056 --> 00:13:06,056
The eye-trees on
its face are fragile.

294
00:13:07,348 --> 00:13:09,889
-(energy booming)
-(Yuji grunting)

295
00:13:09,972 --> 00:13:10,972
What the hell?

296
00:13:11,972 --> 00:13:15,014
Whoa, did I just swap
places with a fish?

297
00:13:15,097 --> 00:13:16,515
(chains rattling)

298
00:13:16,597 --> 00:13:18,474
[Todo] Special-grade
cursed tool!

299
00:13:18,973 --> 00:13:20,973
-(Todo yelling)
-(air whooshing)

300
00:13:21,057 --> 00:13:25,307
(tool crashing)

301
00:13:25,390 --> 00:13:26,307
Playful Cloud!

302
00:13:26,390 --> 00:13:27,848
(blow booming)

303
00:13:27,932 --> 00:13:30,474
(Hanami shouting)

304
00:13:30,557 --> 00:13:32,475
-(Todo gasping)
-(roots booming)

305
00:13:32,558 --> 00:13:33,933
(Todo grunting)

306
00:13:34,016 --> 00:13:35,974
Even a blow from a
special-grade cursed tool

307
00:13:36,058 --> 00:13:40,058
imbued with my cursed
energy didn't take it down?

308
00:13:40,141 --> 00:13:41,141
Huh?

309
00:13:41,225 --> 00:13:43,933
(energy warbling)

310
00:13:44,016 --> 00:13:45,934
(plants crackling)

311
00:13:46,017 --> 00:13:47,892
(Todo gasping)

312
00:13:53,559 --> 00:13:56,017
[Hanami] Plants don't
generate cursed energy,

313
00:13:56,100 --> 00:14:00,018
so I use my left arm to
steal the life from plants

314
00:14:00,101 --> 00:14:03,310
and convert that life
into cursed energy,

315
00:14:03,393 --> 00:14:05,684
(flower squelching)

316
00:14:05,768 --> 00:14:08,143
but that never
gets returned to me,

317
00:14:08,227 --> 00:14:10,935
and instead it all goes
to this flower offering.

318
00:14:11,768 --> 00:14:12,953
I was hoping I wouldn't
have to use this.

319
00:14:12,977 --> 00:14:16,811
(energy crackling)

320
00:14:22,769 --> 00:14:24,520
(footsteps
thudding) [Yuji] Todo!

321
00:14:24,602 --> 00:14:25,353
Stay back, Brother!

322
00:14:25,436 --> 00:14:28,312
Its cursed energy
output is strong!

323
00:14:28,395 --> 00:14:30,187
[Hanami] Yes, but
it will still be easy

324
00:14:30,270 --> 00:14:32,521
for you to avoid
with your technique.

325
00:14:33,686 --> 00:14:35,645
So what shall I do?

326
00:14:36,853 --> 00:14:37,853
Domain Ex-

327
00:14:37,895 --> 00:14:40,188
(explosion booming)

328
00:14:40,271 --> 00:14:42,021
(gasping) It's a veil!

329
00:14:42,104 --> 00:14:45,813
(Todo grunting)

330
00:14:47,146 --> 00:14:50,646
(air whistling)

331
00:14:55,647 --> 00:14:59,814
(energetic electric
guitar music)

332
00:15:01,688 --> 00:15:04,564
(energy crackling)

333
00:15:05,939 --> 00:15:08,606
(Juzou grunting)

334
00:15:09,648 --> 00:15:10,648
Ah, I see!

335
00:15:12,106 --> 00:15:15,023
I wondered why he sounded
so good without the amp.

336
00:15:15,106 --> 00:15:19,065
It's because this old
man himself is the amp!

337
00:15:19,148 --> 00:15:21,440
His technique amplifies
the tune he plays

338
00:15:21,524 --> 00:15:23,483
and launches it
as cursed energy.

339
00:15:24,690 --> 00:15:26,125
But he's a predictable
mid-range fighter,

340
00:15:26,149 --> 00:15:29,774
it's obvious he doesn't
want me getting close to him.

341
00:15:29,857 --> 00:15:32,607
(air whooshing)

342
00:15:32,690 --> 00:15:33,441
Let's make a wallet!

343
00:15:33,525 --> 00:15:36,067
A wallet full of
that old man smell!

344
00:15:36,150 --> 00:15:39,067
(tense music)

345
00:15:39,150 --> 00:15:41,150
(fabric fluttering)

346
00:15:41,234 --> 00:15:43,234
(footsteps thudding)

347
00:15:43,317 --> 00:15:44,442
Roger that.

348
00:15:44,526 --> 00:15:46,400
Keep going, Nishimiya,
and head to Shouko.

349
00:15:46,484 --> 00:15:49,275
(footsteps thudding)

350
00:15:49,359 --> 00:15:51,026
It's okay, Mei has eyes on Miwa.

351
00:15:53,859 --> 00:15:55,609
(air whooshing)

352
00:15:55,692 --> 00:15:57,818
Good thing the veil
didn't cut off my reception,

353
00:15:57,901 --> 00:16:00,734
but I guess that's because
of who the veil was aimed at.

354
00:16:00,818 --> 00:16:02,692
But I'm afraid we have a spy.

355
00:16:02,776 --> 00:16:05,236
Someone's working with
a curse or a curse user.

356
00:16:06,236 --> 00:16:09,486
[Utahime] Looks like
he was right about that.

357
00:16:09,569 --> 00:16:11,319
-Huh?
-(sword whooshing)

358
00:16:11,402 --> 00:16:12,402
Huh?

359
00:16:15,735 --> 00:16:17,416
I thought I cut you
for sure with that one.

360
00:16:19,195 --> 00:16:20,195
[Utahime] A human?

361
00:16:20,278 --> 00:16:22,945
A curse user?

362
00:16:23,028 --> 00:16:24,278
(Haruta sighing)

363
00:16:24,362 --> 00:16:25,903
Always the same old problem.

364
00:16:27,736 --> 00:16:29,694
(energy warbling)

365
00:16:29,778 --> 00:16:31,654
This is nice, isn't it?

366
00:16:33,737 --> 00:16:35,238
Juzou Kumiya made it for me.

367
00:16:36,571 --> 00:16:38,112
I think you met him him earlier.

368
00:16:39,571 --> 00:16:41,488
Your right hand
isn't very strong,

369
00:16:41,612 --> 00:16:44,488
so let the sword's
hand hold yours.

370
00:16:44,571 --> 00:16:46,531
(Haruta chuckling)

371
00:16:46,613 --> 00:16:48,489
(Utahime grunting)

372
00:16:48,572 --> 00:16:51,322
[Haruta] Hm, so what'll
you give me, lady?

373
00:16:51,405 --> 00:16:54,072
[Nobara] I'll bet all the
girls hate you, don't they?

374
00:16:54,155 --> 00:16:55,072
[Haruta] Hm?

375
00:16:55,155 --> 00:16:56,531
Here you meet someone new

376
00:16:56,613 --> 00:16:59,323
and all you do is
talk about yourself!

377
00:16:59,406 --> 00:17:00,406
I'm gonna charge you.

378
00:17:00,490 --> 00:17:02,532
What makes you think
you're a good enough listener

379
00:17:02,614 --> 00:17:04,240
to charge anyone
money for doing it?

380
00:17:04,323 --> 00:17:05,323
(Nobara growling)

381
00:17:05,406 --> 00:17:06,448
Give it a rest!

382
00:17:06,532 --> 00:17:08,864
[Nobara] You always do
this! You pick the worst times

383
00:17:08,948 --> 00:17:09,281
-to start these arguments!
-Hm?

384
00:17:09,365 --> 00:17:11,739
Ah! (laughing)

385
00:17:11,823 --> 00:17:13,865
Wow, who knew I was so popular?

386
00:17:13,949 --> 00:17:16,157
Look at all these
girls, so awesome!

387
00:17:16,241 --> 00:17:18,698
Weren't you listening
to me just a minute ago?

388
00:17:18,782 --> 00:17:20,115
No sweat, I'll cover you.

389
00:17:20,199 --> 00:17:22,324
Careful not to get
caught in the crossfire.

390
00:17:22,407 --> 00:17:24,615
Be careful where you aim!

391
00:17:25,824 --> 00:17:28,033
-(both gasping)
-(air whooshing)

392
00:17:28,116 --> 00:17:30,741
(veil trickling)

393
00:17:32,283 --> 00:17:33,616
The veil's been lifted!

394
00:17:34,658 --> 00:17:36,033
No way!

395
00:17:36,116 --> 00:17:38,575
It hasn't even been
30 minutes yet!

396
00:17:38,658 --> 00:17:39,575
Time to run!

397
00:17:39,658 --> 00:17:41,909
(footsteps thudding)

398
00:17:41,992 --> 00:17:43,576
What was his deal?

399
00:17:43,659 --> 00:17:44,659
So weird.

400
00:17:47,284 --> 00:17:49,576
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

401
00:17:52,284 --> 00:17:55,369
If it isn't my slick new coat
rack floating right up there!

402
00:17:56,494 --> 00:17:58,244
(tense pensive music)

403
00:17:58,327 --> 00:18:01,743
So where should I start?

404
00:18:05,701 --> 00:18:06,701
[Yuji] Huh?

405
00:18:08,495 --> 00:18:11,161
(Hanami grunting)

406
00:18:11,245 --> 00:18:14,161
[Hanami] Looks like
this is as far as we go.

407
00:18:14,245 --> 00:18:15,245
Huh?

408
00:18:15,328 --> 00:18:17,370
Gojo, is that you?

409
00:18:25,412 --> 00:18:26,412
(energy whooshing)

410
00:18:26,496 --> 00:18:29,246
Yuji's on a much higher
level than he was before.

411
00:18:31,412 --> 00:18:32,787
Ah, I see!

412
00:18:32,870 --> 00:18:34,079
Aoi!

413
00:18:34,162 --> 00:18:36,621
Of course he'd be a
great match for Yuji.

414
00:18:36,704 --> 00:18:38,996
Looks like they're
fighting the special-grade,

415
00:18:39,080 --> 00:18:41,330
but I shouldn't have to
worry about them now.

416
00:18:41,413 --> 00:18:43,830
Which means my
priority should be

417
00:18:46,038 --> 00:18:47,830
(air whooshing)

418
00:18:47,913 --> 00:18:48,830
-Hey, you there!
-Hm?

419
00:18:48,913 --> 00:18:49,831
(Juzou laughing)

420
00:18:49,914 --> 00:18:52,664
Coat rack, coat rack, coat rack!

421
00:18:52,747 --> 00:18:53,831
Don't kill him!

422
00:18:53,914 --> 00:18:57,081
(Juzou yelping)

423
00:18:57,164 --> 00:18:58,997
(Juzou grunting)

424
00:18:59,081 --> 00:19:01,664
(stones crashing)

425
00:19:01,747 --> 00:19:03,289
(Juzou groaning)

426
00:19:03,373 --> 00:19:07,623
We have a lot of questions
we need to ask this guy.

427
00:19:07,706 --> 00:19:09,665
Don't let him die on us.

428
00:19:09,748 --> 00:19:11,499
Go on, treat him.

429
00:19:11,582 --> 00:19:14,290
(Yoshinobu growling)

430
00:19:14,374 --> 00:19:16,873
(Gojo gasping)

431
00:19:16,957 --> 00:19:19,291
The guy who was with
Utahime has disappeared.

432
00:19:19,375 --> 00:19:22,208
Guess he must've found
some means of escape.

433
00:19:22,291 --> 00:19:24,291
(air whooshing)

434
00:19:24,375 --> 00:19:26,666
So that just leaves that one.

435
00:19:26,749 --> 00:19:28,250
One adept at running, too.

436
00:19:28,583 --> 00:19:31,917
It's some distance from Yuji.

437
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,000
Oh, well.

438
00:19:34,959 --> 00:19:36,959
Guess I can play a little rough.

439
00:19:37,959 --> 00:19:40,667
Technique Amplification: Blue.

440
00:19:40,750 --> 00:19:42,667
Technique Reversal: Red.

441
00:19:46,793 --> 00:19:47,918
[Hanami] I'm withdrawing.

442
00:19:48,001 --> 00:19:51,335
I'm not arrogant enough to
think I can face Satoru Gojo.

443
00:19:51,418 --> 00:19:52,418
What the hell?

444
00:19:52,460 --> 00:19:55,335
What were you all
trying to do here anyway?

445
00:19:56,793 --> 00:19:58,418
Wait, hold it, Brother!

446
00:19:58,502 --> 00:20:00,253
Why are you stopping me, Todo?

447
00:20:02,169 --> 00:20:03,437
Don't take another step forward,

448
00:20:03,461 --> 00:20:07,127
(energy ringing)

449
00:20:08,002 --> 00:20:09,336
or you'll get caught in it.

450
00:20:09,419 --> 00:20:11,419
(energetic music)

451
00:20:13,587 --> 00:20:14,587
[Gojo] Hollow

452
00:20:15,546 --> 00:20:18,087
(energy booming)

453
00:20:18,170 --> 00:20:19,170
Purple!

454
00:20:20,546 --> 00:20:22,379
(energy booming)

455
00:20:29,505 --> 00:20:33,129
(Hanami yelping)

456
00:20:34,171 --> 00:20:36,712
(Yuji grunting)

457
00:20:43,506 --> 00:20:45,922
(Todo chuckling)

458
00:20:46,005 --> 00:20:48,548
He's just as
nonstandard as ever.

459
00:20:48,630 --> 00:20:50,464
(Yuji moaning in awe)

460
00:20:50,548 --> 00:20:51,797
And now we can't tell

461
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:54,798
if the special-grade
was exorcized or not.

462
00:20:54,881 --> 00:20:56,423
(Juzou wailing)

463
00:20:56,507 --> 00:20:57,507
It hurts!

464
00:20:57,549 --> 00:20:59,798
-It hurts!
-Quiet!

465
00:20:59,881 --> 00:21:00,465
Yay!

466
00:21:00,549 --> 00:21:02,840
That should settle everything!

467
00:21:03,840 --> 00:21:05,798
Or maybe it won't.

468
00:21:05,881 --> 00:21:07,423
(tense music)

469
00:21:09,341 --> 00:21:11,383
(footsteps thudding)

470
00:21:15,466 --> 00:21:18,216
I wonder if Hanami's safe.

471
00:21:19,715 --> 00:21:21,383
Mission accomplished either way.

472
00:21:25,592 --> 00:21:28,842
(closing theme music)

473
00:21:35,633 --> 00:21:38,468
(singer singing in Japanese)

474
00:22:54,639 --> 00:22:57,181
[All] Juju Stroll

475
00:22:57,265 --> 00:22:58,139
[Toge] Salmon.

476
00:22:58,223 --> 00:22:59,723
-(dog barking)
-(cat meowing)

477
00:22:59,807 --> 00:23:01,558
Am I a dog?

478
00:23:01,640 --> 00:23:02,640
No, maybe I like cats.

479
00:23:04,640 --> 00:23:06,723
Although, maybe
if it's a big dog!

480
00:23:08,182 --> 00:23:09,307
All dog.

481
00:23:09,391 --> 00:23:10,640
I think a dog person?

482
00:23:10,723 --> 00:23:11,723
What, really?

483
00:23:11,765 --> 00:23:12,765
No, cats are better!

484
00:23:12,807 --> 00:23:13,724
[Toge] Salmon.

485
00:23:13,808 --> 00:23:15,517
The answer is obviously pandas!

486
00:23:15,600 --> 00:23:18,392
What, you want
me to kill you all?

487
00:23:18,475 --> 00:23:20,559
(Panda roaring)

488
00:23:20,641 --> 00:23:21,659
Everybody hates me, don't they?

489
00:23:21,683 --> 00:23:25,600
I knew it, you all hate me!

490
00:23:25,683 --> 00:23:27,725
Well, there were
only two choices.

491
00:23:27,809 --> 00:23:30,101
Ah, leave it.

492
00:23:30,184 --> 00:23:35,101
(energetic metal music)

